        "kind": "authored-language-rule-and-navigation-policy",
        "navigationPolicy": "signature-first external-consumer definition, not declaration toggle or implementation navigation",
        "explanation": "The paired preceding Wire.fsi exposes render. For this suite external-consumer Go to Definition deliberately targets the public signature declaration, with the implementation range forbidden. F# specifies the public surface, not an editor target: signature-first is an explicit authored product policy, not a claim that the language mandates editor navigation. This preserves the existing signature-boundary consumer target contract; implementation targeting is a policy mismatch here, not necessarily a different semantic symbol.",
        "source": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/fsharp/language-reference/signature-files",
        "policyEvidence": [
          "fixtures/signature-boundaries/expectations.json:create_use -> signature_create_def",
          "crates/navigator-core/src/typeflow.rs:signature_pairs_separate_public_identity_from_definition_toggle"
